{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>Please, Adonai, send by the hand of him whom You will send.</b> It has already been explained above that Moses our master, peace be upon him, was sent to Israel by way of the attribute of justice within the attribute of mercy, and therefore he entreats Him here by this name, which is the attribute of justice, for the attribute of justice is placed within the alef and the yod of the two holy names from which it is vocalized, since both of them are the attribute of mercy — and understand this. And he said, 'by the hand of him whom You will send' — by the hand of the one worthy to be sent, for I am not worthy to speak to the king, and furthermore it is not in keeping with Your honor that Your emissary be of uncircumcised lips. And so Onkelos translated: ביד מאן דכשר למשלח — 'by the hand of one who is fit to be sent.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:56:05.250054376Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}